From d005346d3e595d57ee757fe4513a4a871a7416f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahriar Iravanian <siravan@svtsim.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:45:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] rusticol: pacman runners may apply the amplitude
 reduction

A runner that exports the optional `pacman_runner_v1_run_reduce`
(pacman-runner-v1) also reduces the amplitudes of the selected sum after
its leaves, so that only one value per point comes back from a GPU.

- engine/pacman_runner.rs: `PacmanReduction` (per group, in order, a
  weight and amplitude indices) and the optional symbol; the runner
  reduces when armed and keeps the values. PACMAN_RUNNER_REDUCE=0 keeps
  the reduction in RustiCol.
- evaluator/amplitude.rs: `fill_pacman_reduction` builds the groups of
  `reduce_planes_f64_into_selected_slice` (coherent groups, or a group
  per amplitude, with the selection's weights); not with colour
  contraction.
- engine/evaluation.rs: the selected-sum path
  (run_f64_materialized_selected_direct_into_unprofiled, used by
  `profile` and by `evaluate` of one colour flow) arms the runner and
  takes its values, or reduces as before.
- engine/compiled_direct_prototype.rs: the engine's hooks.

The runner computes the same operations in the same order without FMA,
so the values equal RustiCol's reduction bit for bit. All under the
feature `pacman`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
